eorgia didn't work out he's  still close with Christian barbarac whom  he also met on heartbreak island he says  the two of them planned to explore  business ventures together in the future  including possibly their own line of  vodka Matthew Smith if you've been  concerned about the career of Matthew  Smith the don't worry because he was  already cast in the role he was born to  play  Matthew was cast as Jesus in the short  film that commissioning because well  just look at him  and this isn't the only surprising entry  on his resume he was also a contestant  on the 21st cycle of America's Next Top  Model although you might not recognize  them without his iconic beer he also  made an unbeaten appearance on new girl  in the season 1 finale but there's one  more seemingly random gig we have to  mention Matthew wrote a children's book  it's called windy which is available in  softcover or as an e-book good listener  let's face it not everyone could cope  with the ever-present cameras on too hot  to handle but while there might have  been less drama behind the scenes being  a part of the crew was definitely a  micro calibre dirty job there were six  different cameras in the main bedroom  alone as well as numerous other units  installed all over the house and in  order to keep everyone honest some  unlucky crew members had to watch all of  the footage and they didn't always enjoy  what they saw or heard producer Louise  Peete said crew members had to  investigate suspicious noises or actions  to make sure nobody had broken any rules  apparently one person became an expert  at deciphering rather unpleasant noises  especially in the bathroom that's a  skill that's hard to work into a resume  talent pool creator Laura Gibson knew  that to make the show work she had to  select the right people to join the cast  this was easier said than done since  over 3,000 people auditioned for the  show dealing with thousands of  applicants wasn't easy but there were a  few things in particular producers were  looking for Laura believed that younger  people would have a more difficult time  staying on track while older folks would  keep their eyes on the cash  the older contestants were Bryce and  Matthew who were 29 during the show  while most others were in their early  20s age aside there were some  contestants who really stood out from  the crowd David felt he was everyone's  last boyfriend before they got married  while here he had a list of hookups on  his phone but couldn't put a face to  most of the names francesca got lucky  she didn't even have to send in an  application she was scouted through the  show through her Instagram account and  before she knew it she was skyping with  a producer moderation usually when it  comes to dating shows drinking and drama  go hand in hand with one another but too  hot to handle is the exception to this  because  Kru was surprisingly stingy when it came  to mixing up cocktails for the cast  according to Rhonda they were only  served in moderation so nobody could get  too crazy maybe because it's hard to  hook up with a hangover but alcohol was  surprisingly limited on this show  sleeping arrangements it's no surprise  that many cast members ended up getting  close to each other while working on the  show after all  they all had to share a bedroom creator  Laura Gibson believes this gave them a  chance to see each other in the raw  after all nothing says romance like  finding out if someone's rules in their  sleep or not contestants not only had to  share the same bedroom but they had to  share the same beds while some of them  were fine doubling up on sleeping space  others protested by choosing the floor  instead david admits that he spent more  than one evening stretched out on the  less than comfortable floor eventually  he switched to sharing a bed with his  friend Chiron at least for most nights  all-you-can-eat there was some definite  downsides to appearing on too hot to  handle but let's talk about a major perk  the cast didn't have to contact door -  if they wanted a great meal everyone had  access to a personal chef who prepared  all of their food to order Harry claims  it was the best food he had in his  entire life and nothing was off-limits  they even had the chance to nosh on  deep-fried Oreos apparently there was no  shortage of temptation drama or food  behind the scenes while some cast  members used this as a chance to indulge  francesca preferred to stay on track  when everyone else ordered beef  wellington she stuck with beet  Wellington she feels better on a vegan  diet and the show chef's had no problem  accommodating her requests at the end of  the day the cast was invited to share a  meal together without having the  conversation recorded the catch they  were not allowed to discuss any show  related drama so the audience would miss  out during meal times  Cassatt ow even though some of us binge  watched this show over the course of a  day filming it took a lot longer to hot  to handle was recorded over the course  of 25 days in April 2019 in beautiful  Punta Mita Mexico the cast moved into  the luxurious kasih tau and maybe if  they were footing the bill they would  have been a little more careful not to  break the rules a single night there can  cost a whopping fifteen thousand six  hundred dollars making their twenty five  night stay  three hundred and ninety thousand  dollars cost calculations putting  together too hot to handle definitely  had some unique challenges compared to  other dating shows according to  executive producers Vicki colar and  Jonah Richards one of the most difficult  parts of production was figuring out  appropriate costs for various  transgressions they wanted to ensure  some contestants would break the rules  to make for entertaining television but  they didn't want everyone ignoring the  pot of gold at the end of the rainbow  it was a delicate balance to keep things  interesting without the jackpot getting  totally depleted by a few straight  kisses this was one part of the show  that wasn't decided on in advance  producers wanted to show how far the  cast would go before assigning a dollar  value to their actions  a simple smooch set contestants back  three grand but they could lose up to  $20,000 on a single date working out one  important aspect of reality shows is  cutting contestants off from the outside  world  this means no phones or Internet so  finding ways to spend downtime can be  difficult but luckily for the fitness  buffs in the group David came prepared  it seems the only gym equipment they had  access to was dumbbells which just  wasn't enough  luckily David packed two resistance  bands a jump rope and other Fitness  accessories he could cope with weeks  away from home but not weeks away from  working out he had to get creative but  says he put together a solid routine for  himself and his friends Kells Matt and  Chiron apparently Kel's got really good  at handstand walking which must have  been quite the site inspiration a dating  show with penalties for physical  affection we sail like a crazy idea but  Laura Gibson got inspiration from a  classic source  she was rewatching episodes of Seinfeld  when she came upon one called the  contest in this episode the cast has a  competition to see who can go the  longest without indulging in certain  activities Laura wondered what would  happen if she put real people in a  similar position and decided a dating  show was the best way to find out Lana  of course we appreciate the human cast  members on too hot to handle but let's  not forget to give credit to the  ever-present Alexa escalada Laura loved  the idea of adding an AI robot to make  the show see more  and youthful and to make sure Lauda had  the right personality for the job  producers decided to make her a cross  between Ellen DeGeneres and Mary Poppins  even though Lauda had a lot to say  producers prefer to keep quiet about her  actual mechanics they want to maintain  some magic and mystery regarding Lauda  but allow us to spoil that for you a  little bit apparently Netflix didn't  have the budget for a super-advanced  voyeuristic AI to keep tabs on the cast  Lana may be more than a glorified air  freshener but according to Capital FM  producers tell her what to say and she  repeats it using a digital voice created  by experts what do you think about the  show too hot to handle who's your  favorite cast member and what do you  think the future holds for Matthews  since he's already landed his perfect  movie role let us know if these  behind-the-scenes secrets changed how  you viewed the show in the comment  section and don't forget to click  subscribe for more videos from the  things thanks for watching and we'll see  you again next time

